<title>DENMARK: Rieber has 32.6 pct of Phoenix. [CORRECTED 16:50 GMT]</title>
<headline>Rieber has 32.6 pct of Phoenix. [CORRECTED 16:50 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's Rieber &amp; Son said on Friday that its stake in takeover target Danish Phoenix Contractors had risen to 32.6 percent of equity and 26.7 percent of voting stock.  </p>
<p>The announcement, in a statement to Copenhagen Stock Exchange, came shortly after Phoenix formally recommended its shareholders to accept Rieber's 876 million crown bid for the firm.</p>
<p>Earlier another key suitor, Icopal, whose offer for Phoenix (corrects from &quot;Rieber&quot;) is identical to Rieber's, said it held 11.23 percent of Phoenix's equity and 6.01 percent of voting stock.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
